```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason:  
• `0result.sql` multiplies `num_of_item` by every individual `sale_price` row and then sums, so each item’s price is counted `num_of_item` times – the order value is greatly overstated.  
• `1result.sql` takes only the minimum `sale_price` in each order, understating the order value and also ignores order‑item quantities that differ in price.  
• `2result.sql` derives the order value as `num_of_item × AVG(sale_price)` which is equivalent to summing all sale prices in the order (i.e., a correct total). It then divides that total by the number of orders to get an accurate average order value and applies the correct 2019 registration / purchase filters. Hence `2result.sql` is the only query that follows the stated calculation correctly.